      {
        "file": "NOTES.md",
        "line": 9,
        "text": "**\ud83c\udf89 USB networking works (boot 0076s, 18:24 local): `ping 192.168.7.2` from the PC answers in ~1 ms, 0 % loss (200-packet burst, 1500-byte frames, 512/1024-byte frames).** 0075: CDC-ECM function (bulk 0x81/0x01, interrupt 0x82 NETWORK_CONNECTION; host MAC 02:00:5e:77:ee:01) + kernel ethernet ifnet `ue0` (legacy output, header strip like if_fake) with 192.168.7.2/24 set from the kernel (proto_plumb + SIOCAIFADDR on an in-kernel socket). 0076: received frames into one cluster mbuf (mbuf_allocpacket gave a first mbuf of length 0 -> panic \"Failed mbuf validity check: len -14\"). Host side (Linux cdc_ether, interface `enp0s20f0u3u1`): `nmcli dev set IF managed no; sudo ip addr add 192.168.7.1/24 dev IF; sudo ip link set IF up`. Boot image `shim/out/shim-boot-0076s.img` (`sweetusb=2`). iOS itself does not see ue0 yet (configd needs an IONetworkInterface in IOKit)."
      }
    ],
